EXERCISES={
1:["Identify the input, calculation, output, and safety system in a hypothetical refinery tank controller; which parts should remain operational if the console is disconnected?","Explain the difference between *process temperature* and a digital temperature value; name three possible sources of discrepancy.","Create an interface contract for a switch that closes at most 15 times per minute. Specify active level, voltage, allowable delay, and response to broken wiring.","A sensor reports every 0.5 s. How many expected samples accumulate during a ten-minute shift? Which missing-sample patterns would a simple average conceal?","Describe why a PDP-11 UNIBUS device register and an MSP430 port register are similar programming abstractions but not interchangeable electrical components.","Design a small safe physical analog of a steel-mill inspection station using only a button, LED, and timer. State two limits of the model."],
2:["Trace the accumulator values for a PDP-11 register loop that adds 4, 3, 2, and 1. Record counter and program-counter decisions after each branch.","Convert decimal 63 to octal and hexadecimal, then write its 16-bit binary representation.","State the distinct roles of R6 and R7 on the PDP-11. What would a careless programmer risk by using them as scratch registers?","Explain how (R5)+ differs from R5 and from 4(R5); illustrate all three with a two-word array.","Compare signed and unsigned interpretation of the 16-bit pattern 0xFFFF. What additional status flags matter when interpreting an arithmetic result?","Write a short paper trace that distinguishes a simulated result from a measurement made on actual DEC hardware."],
3:["Assign response deadlines of your own to an emergency input, 100 Hz acquisition loop, and human-readable status report. Justify the deadlines in physical terms.","A timer service takes 150 microseconds every 10 milliseconds. What proportion of execution time does it consume if uninterrupted? Why is utilization not sufficient to prove deadlines?","Explain the difference among latency, jitter, execution duration, and frequency.","Draw a timeline in which a low-priority report is interrupted by a higher-priority input. Mark preemption, resume, and missed deadline if any.","Compare RT-11 and RSX-11M as historical programming environments without suggesting that a bare-metal MSP430 runs either operating system.","Propose one test that measures the distribution of response times instead of reporting only their mean."],
4:["Explain why naming sixteen registers requires four bits and naming eight requires three; describe the effect on a two-operand instruction.","Compare `MOV.W #1,R5` and `ADD.W #1,R5`: do the operations have the same semantics, even if one encoding is shorter?","List the MSP430 special register functions of R0, R1, R2, and R3.","Write equivalent PDP-11 and MSP430 statements for register addition, indexed memory read, and source autoincrement.","Why does the PDP-11 allow more symmetric operand addressing than classic MSP430? Give the instruction-format explanation rather than a marketing label.","Explain why architectural resemblance is insufficient evidence of direct historical descent from DEC to TI."],
5:["Derive the timer output frequency for SMCLK = 1,000,000 Hz and CCR0 = 249, 499, and 999, assuming one toggle each counting interval.","Explain why CCR0=499 means 500 timer ticks rather than 499.","If the meter observes 997 rising edges over 1.001 s, calculate the displayed frequency and signed departure from 1 kHz.","Name at least three ways a measured frequency can differ from the nominal mathematical prediction.","Explain why a one-second gate cannot directly prove a six-microsecond 1-Wire pulse width.","A signal frequency appears stable over five trials. Why might absolute accuracy still be unknown?"],
6:["Show the binary effect of `P1DIR |= BIT0` when P1DIR initially equals 0b01010100.","For a switch tied to ground with a pull-up, write the raw P2.0 bit and logical pressed value in both switch states.","Explain why an LED may be OFF when the corresponding GPIO output latch is high.","Write a pseudocode debouncer and define its sampling interval and acceptance rule.","Contrast a memory-mapped register write with writing to ordinary RAM at the same source-language syntax level.","Propose one physical measurement that can refute an incorrect GPIO schematic assumption."],
7:["Compare the expected edge-to-edge timing of a Timer_A compare output and an ISR-driven GPIO toggle at the same nominal rate.","A periodic task runs every 20 ms and requires 1.5 ms. Calculate its ideal CPU utilization and discuss two limitations of that figure.","Define response time from physical input transition to output change; list the layers through which delay accumulates.","Describe the cost and risk of disabling interrupts around a timing-critical 1-Wire slot.","Provide a reason a polling loop can be preferable to interrupts in a narrow dedicated controller.","Design a repeatable test that reports the worst of 100 measured latencies."],
8:["Sketch the start, eight data, and stop bits of a typical 8N1 UART frame; how many line bit periods does one byte occupy?","At 9600 bit/s, compute approximate duration of a 10-bit 8N1 frame.","What happens when MCU and terminal disagree on baud or voltage level? Distinguish ±12 V RS-232 from 3.3 V UART.","Design a telemetry row including sequence number, raw temperature, validity, and a defined unit.","Explain why an observer PC must not be required to keep the embedded supervisor within its operating policy.","List what a terminal transcript establishes and what it cannot establish about electrical signal quality."],
9:["Draw the three distinct bus actions: drive low, release, and observe; mark the participant responsible for each.","Why can a pin that actively drives high be unsafe on a shared 1-Wire bus?","Explain how pull-up resistance and bus capacitance can affect valid logic timing.","Identify the separate evidence needed for reset, presence, write-one, write-zero, and read slots.","A library assumes an 8 MHz CPU while a project uses 1 MHz. Why is modifying a single delay constant insufficient to certify timing?","Distinguish a meter that measures average frequency from one that measures pulse width and edge timestamps."],
10:["Decode the synthetic raw DS18B20 words 0x01D0 and 0xFF5E as signed Celsius values and then convert them to Fahrenheit.","Why must bytes 0–7 pass CRC comparison with byte 8 before reporting a scratchpad value?","Explain how a valid CRC and a default 85°C representation can coexist with an invalid physical inference.","Separate resolution, repeatability, absolute accuracy, and thermal response time.","Design a comparison test using an independent thermometer and an intentionally changed immersion depth.","What distinguishes a raw integer measurement from a formatted floating-point temperature string?"],
11:["Trace OFF/ON transitions for 27.5, 29.0, 30.0, 29.0, 28.0°C using 30°C ON and 28°C OFF thresholds.","Construct a transition table for exactly 28°C and 30°C in each possible prior state.","Define a fault policy for no sensor, CRC failure, and a stale sample. What evidence would prove each branch executes?","Why should a logical cooling request not be equated with an energized motor?","Explain why test results on a PC can validate a state machine without validating wiring or thermal behavior.","Specify one boundary condition that unit tests routinely overlook."],
12:["Write a defensible claim based on five readings around 1000 Hz; write a stronger claim that would require a calibrated reference.","Calculate mean and range for synthetic frequency values 999, 1000, 998, 1001, 1000 Hz.","List metadata necessary for independent replication after a PC reboot six months later.","Explain how selective deletion of outlier measurements can bias the interpretation.","Distinguish an observed measurement, predicted model value, and formatted dashboard summary.","Develop a one-page evidence checklist for the final temperature-supervisor demonstration."]}

REFERENCE_PAGES=[
('The industrial control system — a reference contract',[
 ('Signals','A transducer output has units, limits, update rate, fault behavior, physical interface, and calibration state.'),('Decisions','A decision maps accepted evidence to states; explicit invalid and stale input states are required.'),('Timing','Specify maximum acceptable response time and identify which system component enforces it.'),('Actuation','An output command is not evidence of physical motion; feedback may be necessary.'),('Safety','Emergency protection and field isolation are outside the capabilities of the introductory LED example.'),('Maintenance','Record revisions, board identifiers, test conditions, and a reproducible commissioning check.')]),
('PDP-11 and MSP430 architecture — quick reference',[
 ('PDP-11 R0–R5','General working registers; R6 stack pointer, R7 program counter.'),('MSP430 R0','Program counter; subject to architecture-specific instruction behavior.'),('MSP430 R1','Stack pointer.'),('MSP430 R2','Status register and certain special operand encodings.'),('MSP430 R3','Constant-generator encodings; not a general storage register.'),('MSP430 R4–R15','General working registers in the classic core.'),('Addressing','Always distinguish programmer-visible syntax from the encoded instruction words.'),('Flags','N, Z, C, and V are useful for program state; flags differ by operation and architecture.')]),
('Bench signals and wiring — commissioning reference',[
 ('MSP430 supply','Use one verified regulated 3.3 V target supply. Never connect a 5 V logic signal.'),('Common ground','Join MSP430 and Pico signal grounds when measuring a common-ended logic signal.'),('Timer output','Custom-board candidate: P1.6/TA0.1, J2 pin 7 → Pico GP3; confirm physical revision.'),('Pico meter','Set source input explicitly and verify STATUS; disable internal waveform generator.'),('UART','P1.2 TX → 3.3 V TTL adapter RX; P1.1 RX ← adapter TX; never attach RS-232 levels.'),('1-Wire','P1.7 candidate, 4.7 kΩ pull-up candidate; inspect the real schematic and assembly.'),('Debugger','Verify external-target Spy-Bi-Wire wiring and isolation jumpers with power removed.')]),
('Frequency and error calculations — ready reference',[
 ('Timer up-mode count','N=CCR0+1 clocks per up-mode period.'),('Toggle output','fout=fSMCLK/[2(CCR0+1)] when one toggle occurs each timer period.'),('Gate estimate','fhat=edge_count/elapsed_seconds; confirm edge type and actual gate measurement.'),('Signed difference','Delta f=fobserved−fnominal.'),('Relative difference','100×Delta f/fnominal percent, when fnominal is nonzero.'),('Spread','Range = maximum observed − minimum observed.'),('Resolution versus accuracy','An extra decimal place does not imply a better timebase or traceable calibration.'),('Reference','An independent suitable reference is required to attribute absolute drift.')]),
('Timing observability and error — ready reference',[
 ('Event time','Timestamp where a specified physical voltage transition is observed.'),('Execution time','Time occupied by a specific code region, not the same as event response time.'),('Latency','Time from stimulus to the corresponding response; specify both boundaries.'),('Jitter','Variation of timing relative to its expected schedule or previous intervals.'),('Pulse width','Elapsed time between leading and trailing edges of one pulse.'),('Frequency','Rate of repetition of a periodic event; frequency alone does not prove pulse width.'),('Uncertainty','Include reference, resolution, clock, software gate, repeatability, and loading concerns.'),('Synchronization','Two instruments with separate clocks may both drift and disagree.')]),
('1-Wire laboratory — commissioning gates',[
 ('Idle','DQ must be high with a suitable pull-up and common reference.'),('Drive low','MCU must sink the line, not assert a high push-pull output later.'),('Release','MCU must stop driving so that the bus resistor can restore logic high.'),('Presence','An observed sensor-dependent pulse in the specified timing window.'),('Write slot','Separate low time for 0 and 1; test with a pulse-width-capable instrument.'),('Read slot','Master initiates, releases, and samples at the correct window.'),('Full conversion','Reset → ROM selection → conversion → wait/verify complete → reset → read scratchpad.'),('Data integrity','CRC of first eight scratchpad bytes compared with the ninth.'),('Physical measurement','Independent thermometer and thermal placement for accuracy claims.')]),
('Supervisor quality assurance — reference',[
 ('OFF','Output state under conditions requiring no cooling request.'),('ON','Output state under conditions requiring cooling request.'),('Hysteresis','Memory of previous valid state between upper and lower thresholds.'),('FAULT','Independent state for invalid, missing, or stale data; physical output action must be specified.'),('Boundary','Test exactly at both threshold values, not only comfortably beyond them.'),('No host','Unplug the observer and verify that local control continues or enters defined behavior.'),('Injected fault','Cause an invalid CRC or missing device and record visible fault response.'),('Hardware output','A logical request must be translated to a verified, protected electrical interface.'),('System safety','Do not present this demonstration as a qualified industrial controller.')])]
